title: Every field has an editor
intro: A field that takes names, lists or anything written like code can't land as a box to type it in any more, and a script's fields get good editors without anyone writing one.
project: Empty | Field Kit Four
write: Scripts/Shop.cs | generic-field-editors/Shop.cs

chapter: A script's lists | Rows, and names with their values
create: Empty
rename: Shopkeeper
add: Shop
explain: field:Shop.Stock | Stock | A script's list is rows now: one thing a row, to set, add, take out and move up.
click: editor:Shop.Stock:add
editorset: Shop.Stock:item:3 = Bow
expectvalue: Shopkeeper.Shop.Stock = Sword\nShield\nBow
explain: field:Shop.Prices | Prices | Lines written as a name and its value are a dictionary: the two side by side, the value a number to drag when they're all numbers.
editorset: Shop.Prices:value:1 = 35
expectvalue: Shopkeeper.Shop.Prices = Sword: 35\nShield: 20
explain: field:Shop.Colors | Colors | And a list of colors is swatches, with the palette to pick from.
key: Ctrl+Z
expectvalue: Shopkeeper.Shop.Prices = Sword: 30\nShield: 20

chapter: Many choices | A key, searched for
explain: field:Shop.Open Key | Open Key | A choice of many, like the key that opens the shop, is searched for by typing a few letters, not scrolled to.
pick: Shop.OpenKey = PageDown
expectvalue: Shopkeeper.Shop.OpenKey = PageDown

chapter: Names and ways | Known from a field's name
explain: field:Shop.Next Scene | Next Scene | A field called Next Scene picks from the project's scenes without being marked, as Prefab and Message fields pick theirs.
pick: Shop.NextScene = Main
expectvalue: Shopkeeper.Shop.NextScene = Main
explain: field:Shop.Facing Direction | Facing Direction | And a direction gets the compass.
click: editor:Shop.FacingDirection:way:Up
expectvalue: Shopkeeper.Shop.FacingDirection.Y = 1
explain: field:Shop.Greeting | Greeting | A field that should stay text says why, here the shopkeeper's own words. Griff's tests fail for any other field typed from memory, saying what to mark it.
